                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fidget box puzzle game - you're given boxes, which you need to figure out the specific logic requirements to 'open' each one.  This is the first game without a story, just puzzle boxes (the second is Access Denied: Escape).\n\nI finished this one in under 2 hours, but admittedly, I wasn't interested in melting my brain on two puzzles, so I did  look up those solutions.  To redeem myself, though, I didn't just take the answer and run with it, I tried to figure out why the answer worked.  I think the thing here is you need to think simple at times, as overthinking things actually may make it harder.\n\nNo bugs or odd issues, or puzzles that don't make sense, but there might be one or two where you need to look closely at things, don't think its all just logic every time. ;)\n\nI enjoyed my time with this one, for the price, I'd say it's worth grabbing, especially if this is your jam.",
